Dear List

Recently I was asked to forward the following message from Hans Zangger 
to this list. In this context I wonder whether there is a need for 
another Debian alpha machine, as a buildd or developer machine? Is there 
a need for a public developer machine? I remeber to have read something 
in the recent past that there are not enough developer machines. Is that 
still the case?

If a there should be an urgent need for any such machine, I am sure to 
find a way to organise its hosting and administration. To point the 
necessity up, some figures about the usage of the current devel machines 
would certainly help (Thanks to Thimo Neubauer and Tim Cutts). From the 
buildd stats I interpret that goetz and goedel get a long.

Regards, Adrian.

